---
import Component from "../../../src/components/pages/SitePageBody.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for SitePageBody — the prose column, carrying one of each
// markdown construct the editor guide actually teaches: sub-headings, a list,
// a link, and the pull quote that gets the crimson bar.
//
// The slot content is hand-written HTML rather than rendered markdown because
// that is exactly what the component receives at runtime: Astro's `render()`
// hands it finished tags, which is why the styles all have to be `:global`.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: SitePageBody</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
    <div id="codeyam-capture" style="padding: var(--space-lg); width: 100%; max-width: 68ch;">
      <Component>
        <p>
          Harvard in Tech connects Harvard alumni, students, and affiliates working across
          technology — founders and engineers, investors and designers, policy people and
          product people.
        </p>
        <h3>How we started</h3>
        <p>
          What began in 2013 as a handful of alumni trading introductions over email is now a
          community of more than 8,000 people across five chapters and two interest-based
          groups.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          The best thing this community ever did for me was a five-minute conversation at a New
          York dinner that turned into my co-founder.
        </blockquote>
        <h3>Getting involved</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Come to something in your city.</li>
          <li>Join the WhatsApp group.</li>
          <li>
            <a href="/volunteer">Volunteer for a project.</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Component>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
